    "title": "<p>Differential diagnosis of nodal T&nbsp;follicular helper cell lymphoma, angioimmunoblastic type</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Ruth Louise Katz",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 658.8pt; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"878\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.85pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Entity</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.45pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"177\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cell infiltrate</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 111.75pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"149\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Expanded FDCs or HEVs</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 122.15pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"163\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Immunophenotype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">T-cell receptor rearrangement</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.45pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"125\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Atypical cells</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Atypical T-zone hyperplasia (seen in viral infections or autoimmune diseases)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"177\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Similar to nTFHL-AI, small and large lymphoid cells, plasma cells, activated lymphoid cells, and immunoblasts</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Presence of tingible-body macrophages</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Absence of FDC hyperplasia; few TFH cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 111.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"149\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 122.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"163\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cells express CD4/CD8, with scattered CD20+, CD25+, and CD30+ cells; CD15&minus;, CD10&minus;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Widespread EBV+ in small lymphoid cells and large immunoblasts</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Few TFH cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Negative</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"125\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&plusmn; Pleomorphic cells resembling HRS cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.85pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Granulomatous lymphadenopathy</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.45pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"177\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Aggregates of epithelioid histiocytes; +/&minus; necrosis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 111.75pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"149\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 122.15pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"163\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Background lymphocytes do not show classic profile of TFH cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Negative</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.45pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"125\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No atypical cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PTCL-NOS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"177\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">May show polymorphic infiltrate similar to nTFHL-AI</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 111.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"149\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No expansion of FDC meshworks and/or proliferation of HEVs</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 122.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"163\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No expansion CD21+ or CD23+ FDC networks</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Positive</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"125\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">EBV+ large B&nbsp;cells are rare</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.85pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PTCL with TFH-cell immunophenotype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.45pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"177\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">May show polymorphic infiltrate similar to nTFHL-AI</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 111.75pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"149\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Some degree of FDC expansion or HEV proliferation can be present</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 122.15pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"163\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">TFH cells positive for CD10, BCL6, CXCL13, ICOS, PD1, and other TFH markers; FDCs CD21+ and/or CD23+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Positive</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.45pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"125\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">EBV+ large B&nbsp;cells may be present</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">NLPHL</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"177\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Large neoplastic LP&nbsp;cells are haphazardly distributed in vague nodules of small lymphocytes</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 111.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"149\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">FDCs within nodules; HEVs usually do not proliferate</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 122.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"163\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Large cells are CD20+, OCT2+, and typically CD30&minus; and EBV&minus;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PD1+ TFH cells may be numerous and form rosettes around LP cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Negative</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"125\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Nuclei of atypical neoplastic LP cells can resemble &ldquo;popcorn&rdquo;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.85pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Classic HL</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.45pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"177\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">HRS cells in a background inflammatory infiltrate including eosinophils; small lymphocytes are not atypical</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 111.75pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"149\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No expansion of FDCs or HEVs</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 122.15pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"163\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">HRS cells positive for CD30, CD15, and PAX5 and often surrounded by T-cell rosettes; TFH cells not increased</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Negative</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.45pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"125\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">HRS cells can be positive for EBV</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">THRLBCL</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"177\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Large neoplastic cells in a background of abundant small lymphocytes and histiocytes; no plasma cells or eosinophils</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 111.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"149\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 122.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"163\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Large B&nbsp;cells are CD20+, CD30&minus;, and EBV&minus;, in a background of reactive T&nbsp;cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Negative</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"125\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Atypical large centroblastoid cells; EBV&minus;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.85pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Hyaline-vascular subtype of Castleman disease</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.45pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"177\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Numerous small lymphocytes without eosinophils; may show regressed lymphoid follicles</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 111.75pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"149\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Prominent vascular proliferation, with proliferation of FDCs in concentric rings</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 122.15pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"163\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Small lymphocytes consist of many B&nbsp;cells and fewer T&nbsp;cells; TFH cells are not increased</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Negative</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.45pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"125\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No atypical cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">FDC, follicular dendritic cell; HEV, high endothelial venule; HL, Hodgkin lymphoma; HRS&nbsp;cell, Hodgkin/Reed&ndash;Sternberg cell; LP&nbsp;cell, lymphocyte-predominant cell; NLPHL, nodular lymphocyte-predominant Hodgkin lymphoma; nTFHL-AI, nodal T&nbsp;follicular helper cell lymphoma, angioimmunoblastic type; PTCL, peripheral T-cell lymphoma; TFH&nbsp;cell, T&nbsp;follicular helper cell; THRLBCL, T-cell/histiocyte&ndash;rich large B-cell lymphoma.</span></p>",
